Ports upstream PR vllm-project/vllm#40371 (open) to this pin.

Adds an opt-in return_progress flag to the OpenAI-compatible chat and
completion endpoints. While a request is still prefilling (chunked
prefill), each SSE chunk may carry a prompt_progress object
(total / cache / processed / time_ms) so clients see prefill progress
on long prompts instead of waiting on a black box. Off by default:
the scheduler emits partial-prefill EngineCoreOutputs only for
requests that set return_progress (plumbed via SamplingParams), and
num_computed_tokens is carried only for those, so other requests pay
no extra cost. The cache field is gated behind the server-side
--enable-prompt-tokens-details flag, like every other cached-token
disclosure in the serving layer.

Adapted to 0.30.0: PromptProgress lives in
entrypoints/serve/engine/protocol.py (the openai/engine/protocol.py
the PR targets no longer exists after the entrypoints reorganisation),
and the scheduler condition lands in the pre-computed
should_emit_output flag.

On 0.31.0: re-cut. outputs.py, the scheduler's output block (its should_emit_output
now also gates the aux-output connector) and output_processor.py moved, and the
hunks follow them; the logic is unchanged.

Kind: feature
What: opt-in return_progress on streaming chat/completions; SSE chunks carry prompt_progress (total/cache/processed/time_ms) while the prompt prefills
Upstream: vllm #40371 (open)
Cut-against: 0.31.0
Retires-when: the pin that carries #40371

